    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d57">

                <pb facs="0067" n="55" sameAs="frus:frus1943v05/pg55"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">033.1110 Wallace, Henry A./14a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Bowers</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-02-18T19:00:00-04:00">February 18, 1943—7
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>176. From the Under Secretary.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d57-f1"/> The President
                    approves the acceptance by the Vice President of the invitation of the Chilean
                    Government to visit Chile. I have, consequently, suggested to the Chilean <pb
                        facs="0068" n="56" xml:id="pg56"/> Ambassador that he personally transmit
                    the official invitation of the Chilean Government to the Vice President, which
                    was arranged to take place today.</p>
                <p>For your personal information you will understand, of course, that the Vice
                    President will have to accept similar invitations from the Governments of the
                    countries through which he will have to pass on his way to Chile. [Welles.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
